Physical chemistry and chemical physics (@physical-chemistry-and-chemical-physics: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_1ZHYBV5NWN4Y4GV6NWPGEKZ7JC
Physical chemistry and chemical physics explain chemical structure, behaviour, and transformation through physical theories and measurements. The material joins thermodynamics, kinetics, equilibrium, quantum states, spectroscopy, statistical mechanics, molecular dynamics, and energy transfer, connecting molecular interactions to experiments and models of reaction conditions, rates, material response, and the limits of chemical change.

**Further common foundation developed:** [Phases, components and constraints](../core/Describe-phases-components-and-the-constraints-on-a-material-sample.lingua) begins the eighth common block. It derives coexistence and conservation, reconstructs a bounded water correlation, reuses materials lessons for common tangents and a symmetric nonideal model, and connects global stability to independent checks and material evidence. The complete physical-chemistry and chemical-physics scope remains pending.

**Parent:** [Chemistry — substances, transformations, and evidence](../Chemistry.lingua#r_2NWJY1HCKPBM4T6YQSDHN8S3S0).
